    summary: "Mitoxantrone was approved in 1987 for acute non-lymphocytic leukaemia in adults in combination with other agents and later for pain relief in advanced hormone-refractory prostate cancer with corticosteroids, where it improved palliative endpoints without extending survival and was then displaced by docetaxel (TAX 327). It remains in AML salvage regimens such as MEC and FLAG-Ida alternatives and in some lymphoma protocols, and carries a separate indication for progressive multiple sclerosis. Cardiotoxicity (lifetime dose limits and ejection fraction monitoring), secondary acute leukaemia and blue-green discolouration of urine and sclerae are characteristic.",
